{{ template "chart.description" . }}

1. **Daily PVC → pod mapping** (`*-daily`) — every Ceph CSI PVC, its PV, the Ceph
   backing object (`pool/image` for RBD, `fsName/subvolume` for CephFS) and every
   pod + `container:mountPath` that mounts it. Read-only against the Kubernetes API.
2. **Weekly orphan report** (`*-weekly`) — Ceph objects with no PV in Kubernetes,
   PVs left `Released`/`Failed`, and RBD trash. Reaches Ceph through the Rook
   **toolbox** or as a direct **client** (for Rook *external mode*).

Pods satisfy Pod Security Standards **restricted**. Requires Kubernetes >= 1.27.

## Install

```sh
helm repo add ceph-reports https://sourcediver42.github.io/ceph-reports
helm repo update
helm install ceph-reports ceph-reports/ceph-reports \
  -n ceph-reports --create-namespace \
  --set smtp.existingSecret=smtp
```

Create the SMTP secret first (or reference an existing one via `smtp.existingSecret`):

```sh
kubectl -n ceph-reports create secret generic smtp \
  --from-literal=SMTP_URL='smtp://smtp.example.com:587' \
  --from-literal=SMTP_USER='user' --from-literal=SMTP_PASS='pass' \
  --from-literal=MAIL_FROM='ceph-reports@example.com' \
  --from-literal=MAIL_TO='you@example.com'
```

Trigger a one-off run: `kubectl -n ceph-reports create job --from=cronjob/ceph-reports-daily test-daily`

## External Ceph (Rook external mode)

Run the weekly job in **client** mode and install the chart **into your Rook
external namespace** so the reused Rook secret and the mon-endpoints ConfigMap are
local (a `secretKeyRef` cannot cross namespaces):

```yaml
weekly:
  ceph:
    mode: client
    autoDiscover: true          # discover pools/filesystems from Ceph
    client:
      image: { repository: quay.io/ceph/ceph, tag: v18 }   # + kubectl, jq, curl, bash, python3
      auth:
        existingSecret: rook-csi-rbd-provisioner
        userIDKey: userID
        userKeyKey: userKey
```

## Ceph access modes

| Mode | How it reaches Ceph | RBAC in Ceph namespace | Use when |
|------|---------------------|------------------------|----------|
| `toolbox` (default) | `kubectl exec` into `deploy/rook-ceph-tools` | `pods`, `pods/exec`, `deployments:get` | Classic Rook |
| `client` | Runs `rbd`/`ceph` in the pod against the mons | `configmaps:get` | Rook external mode |

## Cluster name in the subject

Set `mail.clusterName` (recommended, per environment) so subjects read
`<prefix> [<clusterName>] ...`. Optionally auto-detect from a ConfigMap via
`mail.clusterNameFrom`.

## Email

Reports are sent with a small Python sender (`smtplib`) that attaches the
structured JSON (`mapping.json`; `orphans.json` + `released.json`). Falls back to
`curl` (text only) if `python3` is absent.

## Safety

The weekly job **fails loudly** (non-zero exit + alert email) if a Ceph
pool/filesystem cannot be listed, rather than reporting a false all-clear.

